{
  "_comment": [
    "A trimmed PrizePicks /projections payload, shaped exactly like the real",
    "one: JSON:API, with projections in `data` pointing at players in",
    "`included` through a `new_player` relationship. The league names are the",
    "ones a real payload actually uses -- LoL and VAL, not the long forms.",
    "",
    "The player handles are real handles from the committed roster files, so",
    "running the pipeline against this fixture matches them for real rather",
    "than only proving the parser runs. Every projection below is here to",
    "exercise one branch -- see tests/test_scrape_props.py, which asserts on",
    "each by id. Rosters churn, so a handle here may eventually stop",
    "matching; the end-to-end test rewrites these names from the roster files",
    "at run time and does not depend on any particular player still playing.",
    "",
    "Projection 1013 is the trap: a season-long LoLSZN line on a player who",
    "IS on the roster. It must not match, because a season total compared",
    "against a per-series projection is not a slightly wrong edge but a",
    "meaningless one.",
    "",
    "The real endpoint returns ~35,000 of these across every sport. Six",
    "",
    "The league ids in `included` are ILLUSTRATIVE, not real. Real ones are",
    "provider-side; scripts/dev/inspect_props_payload.py reads them out of a",
    "real payload. They are here so the league-id path in that tool runs.",
    "matching props is enough to prove the shape."
  ],
